From 339fac0985aba8a6c6538f25d2bd45b0528f1755 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 11:30:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 137/145] media: meson: vdec: hevc: tell the esparser a new
 session is resyncing

A stream joined mid-GOP decodes nothing and then stops dead.  Traced on
a 3840x2160 transport stream: seventeen slices are discarded as
pre-IRAP, and from there the firmware sits at HEVC_ACTION_DONE - the
skip command the driver wrote - with the LCU counter at 0, the shifter
byte count frozen, 263 bytes left in the stream FIFO and
esparser_queued_bufs pinned at 17 for as long as the player keeps
trying.  Nothing recovers it, because nothing is broken: the decoder is
waiting for bitstream that will never be written.

Seventeen is twenty CAPTURE buffers minus the three the VP9/HEVC
backpressure gate holds back.  That gate exists so a codec cannot
outrun the CAPTURE queue, and the credit it spends is only repaid by
amvdec_dst_buf_done() - by a decoded frame.  A codec that is discarding
slices produces no frame, so it spends its last credit and stops being
fed, which is precisely why the gate exempts a session that is
resynchronising.

codec_hevc_start() never set that state.  seen_irap is clear from the
kzalloc, so the codec discards slices from the first one, but
sess->resyncing stays 0 and the exemption never applies.  The paths
that resync mid-session - the drain, and stall recovery - both set it
properly; only a session that starts mid-GOP is caught, and it is
caught every time.

Containers that start on a keyframe never reach it: the first slice is
an IRAP, the state clears on that slice, and a credit is repaid by the
frame it produces.  That is why this looked like a 4K problem - the
files that failed were transport streams and the ones that worked were
not.

Fixes: c493d1097b16 ("media: meson: vdec: hevc: keep a resynchronising decoder alive")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
index ed62ad8e3a0c..85ca428bbd2d 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
@@ -977,6 +977,14 @@ static int codec_hevc_start(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 	mutex_init(&hevc->lock);
 	sess->priv = hevc;
 
+	/*
+	 * A session starts knowing nothing, so it discards slices until the
+	 * first IRAP - which is what seen_irap being clear means here.  Say
+	 * so, or the ESPARSER holds this session to the CAPTURE credit it
+	 * has no way of repaying while it is discarding.
+	 */
+	codec_hevc_set_resync(sess, true);
+
 	codec_hevc_hw_init(sess);
 
 	return 0;
